# CAP Legacy Supersede Removal — Caller Migration TODO

After Issue 2 of the red-team fix, the `cap_*_granted_ok` and `cap_*_argflow_ok`
helpers in `oodac/check_cap_grant.oo` no longer accept the broad
`NetCap`/`FsCap`/`SysCap`/`AllocCap` as a supersede for the granular
preferred kind. Callers must declare the granular capability they actually need.

This is a breaking change. The compiler binary must be rebuilt from source for
the new check to take effect. After the rebuild, every caller that uses a
broad cap AND calls a sealed op that requires the granular cap will be
denied by `cap_deny`.

## Migration rules

| Sealed op (granular required) | Broad cap used today | Replace with |
|---|---|---|
| `fetch` / `http_get` / `net_get` / `downloadData` / `query_remote_api` / `net_connect` | `&NetCap` | `&HttpCap` |
| `tcp_connect` / `tcp_write` / `tcp_read` / `tcp_close` / `tls_connect` | `&NetCap` | `&TcpCap` |
| `tcp_bind` | `&NetCap` | `&BindCap` |
| `bind_udp` / `udp_recv` / `udp_send` | `&NetCap` | `&UdpCap` |
| `read_file` / `fs_read` / `path_exists` / `file_size` | `&FsCap` | `&FsReadCap` |
| `write_file` / `fs_write` | `&FsCap` | `&FsWriteCap` |
| `sys_exec` / `process_exec` / `exec` / `spawn_process` / `sys_spawn` / `sys_wait` / `sys_kill` / `lto_xlang_link` | `&SysCap` | `&ProcessCap` |
| `arena_create` / `arena_alloc` / `arena_reset` | `&AllocCap` | `&ArenaCap` |

`&NetCap` is now reserved exclusively for `sock_raw` / `raw_socket` ops.
`&SysCap` is now reserved exclusively for residual OS ops
(`python_embed`, `sys_epoll_create`, `sys_inotify_init`, `sys_prctl`,
`oo_rlimit_set_*`, `landlock_restrict`, `cap_kernel_seal`, `enclave_enter`).
`&AllocCap` is now reserved exclusively for `alloc_bytes` / `free_bytes` /
`malloc` / `free`.

If a function genuinely needs both read and write on the filesystem, it must
take BOTH `&FsReadCap` and `&FsWriteCap` — there is no broad `&FsCap` alias.

## Callers to update

Found 52 files in `oodac/` that take a broad cap. Of those, the following call
a sealed op that requires the granular kind and must be split:

```
oodac/aarch64_ast_main.oo        (read_file, file_size, path_exists)        → FsReadCap
oodac/aarch64_emit_elf.oo        (read_file, write_file, path_exists)       → FsReadCap + FsWriteCap
oodac/aarch64_main.oo            (read_file, file_size, path_exists)        → FsReadCap
oodac/c_cache_store.oo           (read_file, write_file, path_exists)       → FsReadCap + FsWriteCap
oodac/c_emit_lower.oo            (read_file, write_file, path_exists)       → FsReadCap + FsWriteCap
oodac/c_emit_netio.oo            (NetCap, sealed net ops)                   → HttpCap/TcpCap/UdpCap/BindCap
oodac/c_emit_sys.oo              (SysCap, sealed process ops)               → ProcessCap
oodac/check_cache.oo             (read_file, write_file, path_exists)       → FsReadCap + FsWriteCap
oodac/check_cap_grant.oo         (uses bag helpers; no sealed calls directly)
oodac/check_cap_util.oo          (uses bag helpers; no sealed calls directly)
oodac/check_collect.oo           (read_file, path_exists)                   → FsReadCap
oodac/check_mod.oo               (read_file, write_file, path_exists)       → FsReadCap + FsWriteCap
oodac/cli_ast.oo                 (read_file, write_file, path_exists)       → FsReadCap + FsWriteCap
oodac/cli_build_cc.oo            (read_file, write_file, path_exists)       → FsReadCap + FsWriteCap
oodac/cli_build_lto.oo           (read_file, write_file, path_exists)       → FsReadCap + FsWriteCap
oodac/cli_build.oo               (read_file, write_file, path_exists)       → FsReadCap + FsWriteCap
oodac/cli_build_pgo_jit.oo       (read_file, write_file, path_exists)       → FsReadCap + FsWriteCap
oodac/cli_build_pgo.oo           (read_file, write_file, path_exists)       → FsReadCap + FsWriteCap
oodac/cli_build_sovereign.oo     (read_file, write_file, path_exists)       → FsReadCap + FsWriteCap
oodac/cli_build_targets.oo       (read_file, write_file, path_exists)       → FsReadCap + FsWriteCap
oodac/cli_build_x86.oo           (read_file, write_file, path_exists)       → FsReadCap + FsWriteCap
oodac/cli_emit_llvm.oo           (read_file, write_file, path_exists)       → FsReadCap + FsWriteCap
oodac/cli_emit.oo                (read_file, write_file, path_exists)       → FsReadCap + FsWriteCap
oodac/cli_gpu_emit.oo            (read_file, write_file, path_exists)       → FsReadCap + FsWriteCap
oodac/cli_outline.oo             (read_file, write_file, path_exists)       → FsReadCap + FsWriteCap
oodac/cli_parse.oo               (read_file, file_size, path_exists)        → FsReadCap
oodac/cli_reflect.oo             (read_file, write_file, path_exists)       → FsReadCap + FsWriteCap
oodac/cli_repl.oo                (read_file, write_file, path_exists)       → FsReadCap + FsWriteCap
… (and the remaining callers in oodac/, std/, fixtures/, scripts/, …)
```

## Build

After the caller migration, the compiler must be rebuilt:

```
$ bash bootstrap/oodac_pure_build oodac/main.oo oodac_bin.core
```

Until the binary is rebuilt, the old behavior (broad-cap supersede) is still
in effect because the pre-compiled `oodac_bin.core` is older than the source
changes in `oodac/check_cap_grant.oo` and `oodac/check_cap_util.oo`.
